-## Description
+<!-- Generated from deployment/models.catalog.json - edit the catalog, not this file. -->
 
-1D Convolutional Neural Network processing raw high-frequency vibration signals for gearbox bearing fault identification.
+A three-block 1D convolutional network that classifies gearbox bearing condition directly from a raw vibration window, with no hand-built spectral features. It is the highest-resolution view of the drivetrain in the collection: the only model that would consume a real high-frequency DAQ stream unchanged if one were wired to the simulator.
 
-This is model **m01** of the WT-PM wind-turbine predictive-maintenance suite. The repository stays
-independently usable (`python model.py`). The unified **wt-pm** platform wraps the original
-`model.py` through adapter `m01-1dcnn-bearing` — it does not replace or fork this code.
+## How this page fits the collection
+
+The WT-PM collection numbers its 25 repositories **alphabetically 01-25** - that is the number on this page - and gives each one a **task-based adapter id** (`m01-1dcnn-bearing`) used by the platform registry, the `wt-pm` CLI and the fusion engine. Both are printed on every page so the ecosystem graph and the registry can be read against each other.
